00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.262
- Both of my parents were incarcerated.

00:00:14.262 --> 00:00:17.270
Dad had three life sentences.

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:20.430
Mom kept getting locked
up for prostitution so

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.475
my grandma and grandfather raised me.

00:00:24.475 --> 00:00:26.142
- [Interviewer] Wow.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:28.590
How was your childhood?

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.160
- My childhood was good.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.510
My childhood was good.

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:35.860
It was, kinda took us fast
'cause they real old-fashioned.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.880
We didn't get to do
everything everybody else did.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.853
It's like school, church, and home.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:44.053
No going out, nothing.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:47.530
- [Interviewer] Maybe being
with your grandparents

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:49.060
might have been a better move than being

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:50.530
with your real parents.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:52.640
- Yeah, I was gonna say, you know,

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:55.907
things that we didn't get to
do, I'm like, "Wow," you know.

00:00:55.907 --> 00:00:58.257
"When I get to start
knowing things," you know.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:01.510
I'm kinda rebellious, so, yeah,

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:02.950
I'm gonna sneak out the window.

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:04.550
You wouldn't let us do anything.

00:01:05.544 --> 00:01:07.540
- [Interviewer] What were
your parents in prison for?

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:08.373
- My dad was

00:01:11.352 --> 00:01:15.100
